#lang rhombus/static

// `driver.rhm`'s `add_type` routes any non-recursive
// `DatatypeSpec` through `build_nonrecursive_datatype_thms`
// (`datatype_gen.rhm`) instead of `datatype_axioms` (`datatype.rhm`). This
// is the regression test for that wiring: `fixtures/nonrecursive_field_type_ok.rhm`
// declares a non-recursive, field-carrying `type`, a `function` that
// pattern-matches on it, and `theorem`s (including one that is exactly the
// derived `injectivity` statement) proved by `auto()` -- the fact that the
// fixture compiles at all is the proof that the derived `DatatypeThms` are
// usable by everything downstream (rule database, waterfall, `match`
// compilation) exactly like an axiomatic one.

import:
  "fixtures/nonrecursive_field_type_ok.rhm" as t
  "fixtures/two_nonrecursive_types.rhm" as two

check t.swap(t.MkPair(#true, #false)) ~is t.MkPair(#false, #true)
check t.swap(t.swap(t.MkPair(#true, #false))) ~is t.MkPair(#true, #false)
check t.MkPair(#true, #false) is_a t.Pair ~is #true
check:
  match t.MkPair(#true, #false)
  | t.MkPair(a, b): a
  ~is #true

// -- more than one non-recursive datatype in one module ---------------------
//
// Every non-recursive `type` needs `unit`/`prod`/`sum`.  Building that
// algebra per declaration rather than once per session made the *second*
// such declaration in a module fail outright ("type constructor is already
// declared", from `new_basic_type_definition` seeing `unit` twice), which
// nothing exercised until this fixture: `algebra.rhm` now memoizes the
// bootstrap the same way `wfrec.rhm` memoizes `wfrec_rel`, and every
// theory a session builds descends from that one copy.  The fixture
// declaring three such types, and proving theorems about the third from
// the derived injectivity, is the regression test -- it does not compile
// at all otherwise.

check two.turn(two.Left()) ~is two.Right()
check two.turn(two.turn(two.Left())) ~is two.Left()
check two.boxed_colour(two.MkBoxed(two.Red(), two.Left())) ~is two.Red()
check two.MkBoxed(two.Blue(), two.Right()) is_a two.Boxed ~is #true
